 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "sotah.44b.6",
   "daf": "44b",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "״וְהָיָה כְּכַלֹּת הַשֹּׁטְרִים כּוּ׳״. הַאי מִפְּנֵי שֶׁתְּחִילַּת נִיסָה נְפִילָה, מִפְּנֵי שֶׁתְּחִילַּת נְפִילָה נִיסָה מִבְּעֵי לֵיהּ! אֵימָא מִפְּנֵי שֶׁתְּחִילַּת נְפִילָה נִיסָה.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «“And it shall be, when the officers conclude» speaking to the people, that captains of legions shall be appointed at the head of the people” (Deuteronomy 20:9), and that the guards have the license to beat the legs of anyone who attempts to turn back and flee from the war, because the beginning of fleeing is a downfall. The Gemara is puzzled by the language of the mishna: «This» phrase: «Because the beginning of fleeing» is «a downfall,» appears to be backward. The mishna «should have» said the opposite: «Because the beginning of the downfall» is the act of «fleeing.» The Gemara concedes: Indeed, «say» that the mishna means: «Because the beginning of the downfall» is the act of «fleeing.»"
  }
 ],
